MID_SE_Lou_Fia_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Lou_Fia_C_001: ...
MID_SE_Lou_Fia_C_002: Are you here to pray too, Fianna?
MID_SE_Lou_Fia_C_003: I am. I always come here at this time of day.
MID_SE_Lou_Fia_C_004: I come to pray...for Talimun's happiness.
MID_SE_Lou_Fia_C_005: Really? You don't pray for yourself?
MID_SE_Lou_Fia_C_006: No... I think only of Talimun.
MID_SE_Lou_Fia_C_007: Oh! In that case, I'll pray for you! Someone should!
MID_SE_Lou_Fia_C_008: Why would you do that?
MID_SE_Lou_Fia_C_009: You're going through a lot right now. I can hardly\nbelieve you're praying only for the sake of others!
MID_SE_Lou_Fia_C_010: I'm touched by your generosity! It's only natural to\nwant to pray for the well-being of someone like you.
MID_SE_Lou_Fia_C_011: May Fianna's memory return soon, and may the\ndamage to her mind be healed...
MID_SE_Lou_Fia_C_012: Let her rest well and recover quickly... And, and...
MID_SE_Lou_Fia_C_013: That's plenty, Ludia. I could ask for nothing more.
MID_SE_Lou_Fia_C_014: You're a kind soul. Thank you.
MID_SE_Lou_Fia_C_015: I'm glad to have a friend like you.
MID_SE_Lou_Fia_C_016: I feel the same way!
MID_SE_Lou_Fia_C_017: {SetColor=Gray}She's so sweet and pure... I hope she can survive\nworking for this company.{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Lou_Fia_C_018: {SetColor=Gray}Talimun makes some unreasonable requests,\nand Ursula can be strict...{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Lou_Fia_C_019: Um... Ludia? Is everything alright?
MID_SE_Lou_Fia_C_020: Oh! Just...if you ever have any trouble, please know\nthat you can come to me anytime!
MID_SE_Lou_Fia_C_021: I'll make sure you're taken care of no matter what\nhappens, Fianna. You can lean on me all you need!
MID_SE_Lou_Fia_C_022: Ah... I see. I appreciate that.
MID_SE_Lou_Fia_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Lou_Fia_B_001: Oh! Hello, Fianna!
MID_SE_Lou_Fia_B_002: Hello... I hope you're well, Ludia.
MID_SE_Lou_Fia_B_003: I actually just got back from a trip into town to check\nout some of the latest fashions.
MID_SE_Lou_Fia_B_004: Plus, a popular candymaker came out with some new\ntreats, and they're the talk of the town.
MID_SE_Lou_Fia_B_005: When the war first started, there was concern over\nsupply levels, but everyone seems to be doing well!
MID_SE_Lou_Fia_B_006: After that, I... Oh. I haven't let you get a word\nin edgewise. I hope I'm not boring you...
MID_SE_Lou_Fia_B_007: Oh, no! I was happy listening. You lead an\ninteresting life, Ludia.
MID_SE_Lou_Fia_B_008: Ahaha. I was just saying what I saw in the city.
MID_SE_Lou_Fia_B_009: Hey, I know! Why don't we go out into town\ntogether sometime?
MID_SE_Lou_Fia_B_010: Well, I, uh...
MID_SE_Lou_Fia_B_011: Sorry, I didn't mean to put you on the spot.
MID_SE_Lou_Fia_B_012: Oh... That's not it. It's just that, well...
MID_SE_Lou_Fia_B_013: I was thinking I might want to look for a gift.\nFor you, I mean...
MID_SE_Lou_Fia_B_014: For me? I haven't done anything to merit a gift.
MID_SE_Lou_Fia_B_015: You always come visit with me, wanting to help me\nsomehow or another. That is reason enough.
MID_SE_Lou_Fia_B_016: In that case, why don't we go together? I wouldn't\nwant you to have to go alone!
MID_SE_Lou_Fia_B_017: I couldn't stand if something were to happen to you\nwhile you were out in town on my account.
MID_SE_Lou_Fia_B_018: You are too kind to worry over me so, Ludia.\nI feel almost like your little sister.
MID_SE_Lou_Fia_B_019: What? I'm the older sister?!
MID_SE_Lou_Fia_B_020: Of course. You know so much of the world, you keep\nwatch over me... I can count on you for anything.
MID_SE_Lou_Fia_B_021: This is a little embarrassing. I'm the youngest in\nmy family, so I've never been told that before.
MID_SE_Lou_Fia_B_022: Does that mean you're going to call me Big Sister\nfrom now on?
MID_SE_Lou_Fia_B_023: Hehehe. I just might, Big Sister.
MID_SE_Lou_Fia_B_024: Hey! Y'know, I kinda like the sound of that!
